# Reconnaissance scratch — never commit raw fetch bodies.
#
# NOTE ON PATHS: this file sits at .hermes/recon/, so patterns are relative to
# THAT directory. The first version used ".hermes/recon/**", which can never
# match from here and silently ignored nothing — `git check-ignore` returns no
# match. That is a dangerous failure mode for an ignore rule: it looks like
# protection and is not.
#
# Rationale for ignoring: the recon lenses download many MB of raw HTTP bodies
# (HTML, parquet, XLSX, PDF). Those are scratch, not source. Committing them to
# this PUBLIC repo adds ~22MB of third-party content and hundreds of thousands of
# lines, trips the global pre-push guard on false positives (scraped CSS class
# names match the dashed-token shape the guard looks for; scraped pages also carry
# phone-shaped strings and absolute paths), and makes the repo a redistribution
# point for material the project does not own.
#
# What IS committed: the written findings (*.md), the probe ledger
# (*-results.jsonl) and the small probe scripts — the evidence, which is ours.

# Whole capture directories.
2026-09-20/raw/
2026-09-20/l1/
2026-09-20/l1b/

# Raw response bodies and command output by extension, anywhere below here.
**/*.body
**/*.out
**/*.err
**/*.body.txt

# Bulk artifacts pulled while probing.
**/*.csv
**/*.pdf

# Any future dated capture dir keeps the same shape.
*/raw/
*/l1/
*/l1b/
